## D2 IMPACT ADJUDICATION SUMMARY

Retained BAT-001 and REQ-014 as confirmed impacts. Retained review candidates for BMS, charger, enclosure, cooling plate, frame, REQ-003, REQ-008, and the released BOM/product configuration because the evidence supports specific compatibility or lifecycle checks for the changed battery.

The lifecycle completeness audit also identified MFG-001 and MFG-002: both are battery-pack assembly operations, so their applicability to the changed capacity configuration merits review. No evidence-supported validation-test entity was returned.

Removed CAB-001 and CON-001 because the capacity change does not establish a current or interface change. Removed SUP-001 because approved supplier status alone does not establish a sourcing or qualification impact; removed SW-001 and SNS-001 because their relationships to the BMS do not show that the change affects their behavior. Historical service records remain context-only. REQ-008 is retained only for mass-limit verification; no mass increase is established.

Major uncertainty remains the proposed pack’s dimensions, mass, electrical and thermal characteristics, and revision. No validation results for the changed configuration were provided.

